  "instance_name": "Native_American_identity_as_shield",
  "label": "Native American identity as a shield against criticism",
  "description": "The meme uses the assertion 'I'm Native American' as a rhetorical device to dismiss or deflect criticism, implying that one's ethnic or cultural identity grants them moral or social immunity. This is a harmful trope that reduces complex cultural identities to simplistic defensive tools, often used to provoke or belittle others. It relies on the real-world understanding that identity can be weaponized in social discourse.",
